i'm alvin i'm a tasty producer and i  made a giant 30 pound burger it was kind  of a crazy thing because it required me  to think about all the components such  as the bun the burger and the cheese and  first thing i did was think about how do  i tackle the bun i settled on a pretty  standard brioche recipe but the tricky  thing was that we had to multiply it by  like 10. essentially just added a lot of  eggs butter and water into a mixing bowl  this was actually multiplied so much  that it was supposed to make like a  giant brioche loaf and usually with  brioche you cut it up and then you eat  it but for this one you just roll it up  and you bake it off as the whole thing  it was actually really fun i've never  made brioche before so this is a cool  experience but what was super awesome  about this one was that i was able to  just play with the dough it was just so  soft it was super elastic and i just  wanted to kind of hold it forever  because it was like holding a newborn  baby and i think when my kid grows up i  don't want him to grow up because i  wanted to feel like that for a long time  i expected it to expand a lot and we  just kind of diy this foil ring and kind  of had that the size of the hamburger  bun so it was kind of nice to have like  a finished almost biscuit-like looking  brioche so after cutting in half it was  pretty awesome we buttered it just  because i don't think you want a burger  that doesn't have a toasted bun and then  we approached the meat so the meat was  pretty interesting because it was  essentially two giant patties i didn't  want to do one super thick patty because  i don't think you can really eat it and  i really was inspired by a lot of the  smash burger style burgers we've seen  out there so i wanted to do two thin  patties and that required me to pretty  much go to the grocery store and go to  the ground beef section and essentially  clean it out definitely got a lot of  weird looks some old lady was super nice  was really cute she was like oh young  man you must be a growing boy and i was  like uh yeah yeah sure and she was like  oh i have a son and he used to eat just  like you and i was like if he ate like  this  i i'm a little worried about that so you  know it could have been pretty easy to  just throw a bunch of cheese slices on  the burger you know i didn't really want  to play that game i kind of mixed  together you know american cheese slices  chopped it up mixed it with another  cheese that i really like which is  cheddar cause i wanted the flavor and i  think cheddar tastes really good so i  melted them together and kind of created  like this cheese concoction mixture  which was really satisfying by the way  but i was like cutting cheese for like  20 minutes because there's so much  cheese that went into this it was like  40 blocks after that just made you know  kind of  i was like hey if you spread it on a  tray in a square shape and you trim it  will you end up with a swerve cheese we  got a nice firm american slice i was  like oh wow this actually turned out  pretty well assembly was really tricky  because usually when you're assembling a  burger you don't think about how heavy  everything is it was like three whole  tomatoes and two containers of lettuce  to fill that burger up it was just a lot  of stuff all around i pretty much only  had one attempt i was really happy with  it because when you are doing it and  you're so close with it it doesn't look  like much but when you step back and  look at that in its entirety after that  obviously you had to make some of that  burger secret sauce that you spit on the  bun it's really simple mayo ketchup  mustard a little bit of pickle juice  i really enjoyed making this one it was  just really fun adventure i thought it  looked beautiful and was able to  surprise my good friend victor with it  and he was super crazy about it that is  the adventure of a 30 pound breaker  i'm alexis and i'm going to make a  classic diner style burger with pickled  red onions and homemade aioli to make  the pickled bread onions i'm going to  bring apple cider vinegar sugar and salt  to a boil remove it from the heat add  the onions and let it sit for an hour at  room temperature while the onions are  pickling i'm going to make my aioli you  add an egg yolk dijon mustard garlic  whisk them together and then i'm slowly  going to add the olive oil until it  begins to emulsify and at the end it  should be thick and creamy once you add  the lemon juice the aioli will become  paler in color salt to taste aioli will  keep up for two days in the fridge but  after that you want to throw it away i'm  going to butter the buns with melted  butter and then put them under the  broiler for a minute and a half so they  just get just a little toasted for diner  style burgers and you just want to take  about a four ounce piece of ground beef  roughly shape it into a mound i think  like a glorified meatball i'm seasoning  the meat with salt and pepper and then  i'm going to get the cast iron really  hot a little bit of oil and then i'm  going to add the  meat mounds and then immediately smash  it down with a spatula  diner style patties cook really quickly  it should be about two to three minutes  on this side as soon as i flip the  burger i'm adding the cheddar cheese by  the time the cheddar cheese has melted  the burger should be done cooking it's  got the perfect combination of pickles  from the red onions it's got that creamy  aioli to go with the really juicy meat  and then melted cheese a thin diner  style patty is classic all-american and  it's really easy to make at home i just  made my dream burger  [Music]  [Music]  you
 

